CORRECT: include idempotencyKey in every mutating RPC
```

### What should a senior engineer know?

Never retry non-idempotent mutations blindly. Retries and hedging can multiply load on a struggling service. Prefer a service mesh for consistent, language-agnostic policy across many services. The combination of deadlines with propagation, typed status codes, and declarative retries is what makes gRPC reliability first-class rather than bolted-on.
